{
  "rationale": "The plant separates sensing (uncontrollable obstacle events) from motion (controllable pulses). The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions: move_forward/random_walk in clear, rotate_clockwise for left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles, and move_backward for front obstacles. Recovery is brief and returns to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated front blockage. All uncontrollable events are total in every state. Only one controllable is enabled per action state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion capabilities",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased recovery and exploration logic"
  ],
  "G": [
    {
      "name": "G1",
      "purpose": "Models robot's perception: obstacle and clear events from sensors",
